# Data pipeline

{% if ingestion_mode == 'batch' %}
The selected batch workflow reads JSON files from a Unity Catalog volume into a Bronze
materialized view.
{% else %}
The selected arriving-file workflow uses Auto Loader to ingest immutable JSON files
from a governed volume into a streaming Bronze table.
{% endif %} Silver drops missing timestamps and invalid numeric inputs, fails missing IDs,
and warns on missing labels. Gold fails duplicate IDs and builds model-ready features.
Inspect Lakeflow expectation metrics for violation counts. Raw records stay in Bronze;
this example uses warn/drop/fail and does not implement a separate quarantine table.

The arriving-files option uses Auto Loader into a streaming Bronze table and batch
materialized views downstream. Refreshes run on the job schedule; this is incremental
file ingestion, not an always-on service. Pipeline-managed checkpoints belong to the
pipeline. Keep input files immutable. Changing batch to streaming after deployment
requires a migration or a new pipeline/table name.

Local pandas transformations exercise the same contract; the PySpark adapter must
also pass the DEV workflow before a release is considered remotely verified.
